{"tool_name":"sbml2hyb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"sbml2hyb","home":"https://github.com/r-costa/sbml2hyb","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Python interface for Systems Biology Markup Language (SBML) compatible hybrid modelling.","addition_date":"2023-11-07T10:58:51.166314Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:33:10.762197Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Desktop application","Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:sbml2hyb","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"rs.costa@fct.unl.pt","name":"Rafael S Costa","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7539-488X","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Jos\u00e9 Pinto","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Jo\u00e3o Ramos","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Leonardo Alexandre","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Rui Oliveira","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Aggregation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3436"},{"term":"Format validation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0336"},{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"}]}],"name":"sbml2hyb","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btad044","metadata":{"abstract":"Here, we present sbml2hyb, an easy-to-use standalone Python tool that facilitates the conversion of existing mechanistic models of biological systems in Systems Biology Markup Language (SBML) into hybrid semiparametric models that combine mechanistic functions with machine learning (ML). The so-formed hybrid models can be trained and stored back in databases in SBML format. The tool supports a user-friendly export interface with an internal format validator. Two case studies illustrate the use of the sbml2hyb tool. Additionally, we describe HMOD, a new model format designed to support and facilitate hybrid models building. It aggregates the mechanistic model information with the ML information and follows as close as possible the SBML rules. We expect the sbml2hyb tool and HMOD to greatly facilitate the widespread usage of hybrid modeling techniques for biological systems analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Alexandre L."},{"name":"Costa R.S."},{"name":"Oliveira R."},{"name":"Pinto J."},{"name":"Ramos J."}],"citationCount":4,"date":"2023-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"SBML2HYB: a Python interface for SBML compatible hybrid modeling"},"pmcid":"PMC9889961","pmid":"36661327"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Systems biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2259"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"sbml2hyb","home":"https://bio.tools/sbml2hyb","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Python interface for Systems Biology Markup Language (SBML) compatible hybrid modelling.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:sbml2hyb/app/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":2,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"2024"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btad044","pmcid":"PMC9889961","pmid":"36661327","ref_count":18,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":1,"year":"2001"},{"count":1,"year":"2003"},{"count":1,"year":"2004"},{"count":1,"year":"2008"},{"count":1,"year":"2012"},{"count":1,"year":"2016"},{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":2,"year":"2006"},{"count":2,"year":"2019"},{"count":2,"year":"2020"},{"count":3,"year":"2011"}],"title":"SBML2HYB: a Python interface for SBML compatible hybrid modeling.","year":2023}]}],"summary":{"description":tru